# PR Creation Workflow

When creating a pull request (Option 2 of **finishing-a-development-branch**):

1. **Assess changes** — Inspect uncommitted and committed-but-not-pushed changes. Divide logically (feature vs docs vs chore). Separate branches and PRs per group.
2. Create branch, commit, push — **Use `ai/` prefix** (e.g. `ai/feature-name`) so the auto-PR workflow creates the PR from conventional commits.
3. Create PR — follow [.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md](.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md)
4. **Checkout main and pull** — `git checkout main && git pull`

Workflow pins are automated: [update-workflow-pins](.github/workflows/update-workflow-pins.yml) runs on push to main when workflows/actions change. No manual step.

Do not finish until step 4 is done. Workspace must be left on `main`.
